   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Aid</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Vector Surveillance and Control in the Indo-Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment will strengthen the capacity of partner countries in the Indo-Pacific to anticipate, prevent, detect and respond to vector-borne disease threats. Activities under this investment target malaria, dengue, and other mosquito-borne illnesses. Activities aim to strengthen partner governments&apos; vector surveillance and control systems and include: vector surveillance data collection and analysis, vector staff workforce development, improved data management and data use for decision making, enhanced strategic planning, and strengthened health systems. An innovative approach to dengue control, the Wolbachia method, is also supported in select priority countries. The investment comprises three separate but complementary programs. Program partners recognise the importance of integrating GEDSI, climate change, One Health and local leadership considerations.</narrative>
  </description>
